Run from the repository root:

    python3 test/run_tests.py

Requires Python 3 and a C++11 compiler with AddressSanitizer and UBSan support.
CXX can override the compiler. No Arduino hardware or third-party Python packages are needed.

protocol_test.cpp compiles the same rgp_protocol.cpp used by ESP32 firmware.
It reads all three unmodified supplied vector files and reports the distinction
between ESP behavior, CRC checks, unsupported optional capability contexts, and
PC-side examples (valid framing round trip only, not host semantic validation).

firmware_test.cpp compiles the real main.cpp setup/loop with deterministic doubles
for Arduino, I2C, ADS1115, ImuManager, and Orientation. It tests application scheduling,
input gating, calibration, recovery, scanning, and actual RGP output. The doubles
are not tests of physical hardware, FastIMU drivers, or orientation filter accuracy.
Both executables run with AddressSanitizer/UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.

Vectors were copied unchanged from the user-supplied RGP/test-vectors directory
(RGP/1 1.0 release candidate, two-player TEL revision) on 2026-10-15.
